{
  "explanation": "The attacker is attempting a password spray attack against the SSH service, rotating through different target usernames ('ops', 'maria', 'jenkins') and slightly varied source IPs within the same subnet to bypass standard single-IP rate limits. The multiple failed login attempts indicate that the authentication phase is actively being probed, though no successful compromise is shown in the provided logs.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Block the attacking IP address (222.186.30.5) and associated subnet at the firewall or network perimeter.",
    "Disable password-based authentication for SSH and enforce secure SSH key-based authentication.",
    "Implement automated IP banning tools such as Fail2ban to dynamically block sources exhibiting repeated authentication failures."
  ]
}
